      "title": "Diagnosing Notification Hub Delivery Failures due to Third-Party Dependencies",
      "content_summary": "Guidance on troubleshooting upstream dependency issues, API deprecations, and credential failures that prevent notification delivery.",
      "content_body": "When notification delivery fails or times out, first check vendor status pages for known incidents affecting SMS or push providers. Verify that API keys are valid and not expired, as credential issues often manifest as timeout errors. Ensure system clocks are synchronized to prevent authentication rejects from upstream services. If a version conflict or deprecation is suspected, review recent dependency updates and rotate credentials if necessary. Escalate to engineering if vendor engagement does not resolve the underlying dependency failure."
